From: dtrace.nix maintainers
Subject: tests: fix portable postprocessing and disassembly synchronization

The postprocessors intend to remove a symbol offset beginning with "+0x".
An unescaped leading plus is not a valid extended regular expression in
modern gawk, so the postprocessor itself fails before it can assess DTrace's
output.

The trampoline annotation test relies on BEGIN to terminate DTrace.  BEGIN can
fire before the later io trampoline has been emitted under slow emulation.  Use
the -c synchronization point instead: DTrace starts the child only after probe
enablement is complete, then exits when the child terminates.

The FBT stress tests intend to check entry and return arguments and a nested
call, but their empty function fields attach to every FBT probe in the kernel.
Contemporary generic kernels expose more than 150,000 such probes, turning
functional checks into accidental multi-gigabyte scalability tests.  Trace
vfs_read, which the DTrace consumer itself exercises, and its rw_verify_area
call.  This also ports the tail-call case away from the obsolete ioctl symbol.
Use a global readiness flag where the selected probe is independent of the
thread that delivered tick-1.

diff --git a/test/unittest/stack/tst.stack_fbt.sh b/test/unittest/stack/tst.stack_fbt.sh
index 6275646c..ef5a56ea 100755
--- a/test/unittest/stack/tst.stack_fbt.sh
+++ b/test/unittest/stack/tst.stack_fbt.sh
@@ -43,6 +43,6 @@ fi
 awk 'NF != 0 { sub("\\.constprop\\.[0-9]", "");
                sub("_after_hwframe\\+", "+");
-               sub(/+0x[0-9a-f]*$/, "");
+               sub(/\+0x[0-9a-f]*$/, "");
                sub(/^ */, "");
                print }' dtrace.out > dtrace.post
 if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then
diff --git a/test/unittest/variables/bvar/check_caller_to_stack2.awk b/test/unittest/variables/bvar/check_caller_to_stack2.awk
index 8499852a..5527a610 100755
--- a/test/unittest/variables/bvar/check_caller_to_stack2.awk
+++ b/test/unittest/variables/bvar/check_caller_to_stack2.awk
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@ NF != 0 {
 
 	# Now we have the caller frame.  Strip off the offset.
 	expect=$1
-	sub("+0x[0-9a-f]*$", "", expect);
+	sub("\\+0x[0-9a-f]*$", "", expect);
 
 	# Finally, get the sym(caller) output.
 	if (getline != 1) { print "ERROR: missing expected output"; exit(1); }

diff --git a/test/unittest/disasm/tst.ann-tramp-lvar.sh b/test/unittest/disasm/tst.ann-tramp-lvar.sh
--- a/test/unittest/disasm/tst.ann-tramp-lvar.sh
+++ b/test/unittest/disasm/tst.ann-tramp-lvar.sh
@@ -7,21 +7,37 @@
 #
 
 dtrace=$1
+raw=$tmpdir/ann-tramp-lvar.raw
 
-$dtrace $dt_flags -xdisasm=2 -Sn '
-BEGIN,
+if ! $dtrace $dt_flags -xdisasm=2 -Sn '
+proc:::exit,
 io:::start
+/pid == $target/
 {
 	exit(0);
 }
-' 2>&1 | gawk '/this->/ {
+' -c /bin/true >"$raw" 2>&1; then
+	cat "$raw"
+	exit 1
+fi
+
+if ! gawk '/this->/ {
 		sub(/^[^:]+: /, "");
 
 		gsub(/%r[0-9]/, "%rX");
 		$2 = "N";
 		$3 = "N";
 
+		found = 1;
 		print;
-         }'
+         }
+
+         END {
+		if (!found)
+			exit 1;
+         }' "$raw"; then
+	cat "$raw"
+	exit 1
+fi
 
-exit $?
+exit 0
